      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-7221",
      ":question/problem": "The acceleration $a$ at time $t$ of a particle $P$ moving in the $xy$-plane is given by\n\n$$\na(t)=\u27e86t-2,4\u27e9.\n$$\n\nGiven that the particle is at the position $(0,0)$ and has velocity $\u27e81,\\,4\u27e9$ when $t=1,$ calculate the position vector of $P$ at time $t.$"
    },
    {
      ":db/id": 17592186079197,
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/type": {
                ":db/ident": ":answer.type/math"
              },
              ":answer/value": "r = \u27e8\\frac{1}{4}t^{3} + 2t, \\frac{1}{6}t^{4} + t\u27e9",
              ":db/id": 17592186077961
            },
            {
              ":answer/type": {
                ":db/ident": ":answer.type/math"
              },
              ":answer/value": "r = \u27e8\\frac{1}{6}t^{3} + 4, \\frac{1}{12}t^{4} + 2\u27e9",
              ":db/id": 17592186077962
            },
            {
              ":answer/type": {
                ":db/ident": ":answer.type/math"
              },
              ":answer/value": "r = \u27e8\\frac{1}{6}t^{3} + t, \\frac{1}{12}t^{4} + 2t\u27e9",
              ":db/id": 17592186077963
            },
            {
              ":answer/type": {
                ":db/ident": ":answer.type/math"
              },
              ":answer/value": "r = \u27e8\\frac{1}{6}t^{3} + 2t, \\frac{1}{6}(t^{4} + 2t)\u27e9",
              ":db/id": 17592186077964
            },
            {
              ":answer/type": {
                ":db/ident": ":answer.type/math"
              },
              ":answer/value": "r = \u27e8\\frac{1}{4}(t^{3} + t), \\frac{1}{12}t^{4} + 2t + 3\u27e9",
              ":db/id": 17592186077965
            }
          ],
          ":answer-field/key": "selection",
          ":answer-field/type": {
            ":db/ident": ":answer-field.type/radio"
          },
